on a material obligation","kind":"finance","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000119312524248692/0001193125-24-248692-index.htm"},{"date":"2024-10-03","form":"8-K","codes":["8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000114036124042757/0001140361-24-042757-index.htm"},{"date":"2024-09-17","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000201164124000003/0002011641-24-000003-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["Ferguson Enterprises Inc. /DE/ files with the SEC under \"Wholesale-Hardware & Plumbing & Heating Equipment & Supplies\", based in VA, and has been publicly reporting for 2 years.","It reported $29.7bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 3.6% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 31.0%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($2.4bn of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Growth has been positive in 4 of the last 5 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000201164126000030/0002011641-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0002011641-26-000030"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $2.4bn over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000201164126000030/0002011641-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0002011641-26-000030"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-2.1% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000201164126000030/0002011641-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0002011641-26-000030"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue grew only 3.6% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000201164126000030/0002011641-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0002011641-26-000030"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.2% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011641/000157280626000004/0001572806-26-000004-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 23.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.23,"consecutive":2,"current":0.31,"current_display":"31.0%","threshold_display":"23.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -11.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.11,"consecutive":2,"current":0.036,"current_display":"3.6%","threshold_display":"-11.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","thres